vLLM 0.32.0: let Qwen3.5 use a quantized (int8) token embedding

vLLM ships CompressedTensorsEmbeddingWNA16Int (dequant-on-gather), but the
qwen3_5 model code never passes quant_config to VocabParallelEmbedding, so a
checkpoint whose embed_tokens is int8 group-128 loads the dense copy instead
(and the pack-quantized tensors go unused). Same two-line idea as the upstream
syv-ai patch; here only the target model needs it because the MTP drafter
shares the target embedding (see the share-heads patch).

Pairs with tools/quantize_token_tables.py. Apply from site-packages: patch -p1

--- a/vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3_5.py
+++ b/vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3_5.py
@@ -248,9 +248,14 @@
 
         self.vocab_size = config.vocab_size
 
+        # Route the token table through vLLM's quantized-embedding path when the
+        # checkpoint quantizes it (int8 group-128). Without quant_config the
+        # loader keeps the bf16 copy and the int8 savings are lost.
         self.embed_tokens = VocabParallelEmbedding(
             self.vocab_size,
             config.hidden_size,
+            quant_config=self.quant_config,
+            prefix=maybe_prefix(prefix, "embed_tokens"),
         )
 
         def get_layer(prefix: str):
